    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.3,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.2,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.3 from 7 h onward, which is what saturation would also look like. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test this. The 10x dilution read 0.1264, which scales to 1.26. The 3x dilution read 0.4705, which scales to 1.41. The undiluted reading was 1.29. If the reader were saturating, the diluted readings scaled back up should be clearly and consistently higher than 1.29, and the 10x dilution should be the highest. Instead the 10x value is slightly below 1.29, and the 3x value is only about 9% above it. That pattern fits replicate noise, which is a few percent per read in the plateau data. I had one replicate per dilution, so the evidence is limited. It indicates a true stationary-phase OD of about 1.3, in the range where the reader is roughly linear."
  },
